## 2. NON-NEGOTIABLE DEVELOPMENT RULES

1. Inspect the entire existing source code before implementing changes.
2. Preserve all existing working features and business functionality.
3. Preserve the existing corporate branding, animated technology backgrounds, logos, and visual identity.
4. Do not replace the existing application with a generic template.
5. Do not introduce duplicate components, conflicting routes, redundant database tables, or parallel authentication systems.
6. Do not remove working features simply to eliminate compilation errors.
7. Never hardcode API keys, passwords, private tokens, or production credentials.
8. Never expose server-side secrets in frontend bundles.
9. Never fabricate successful transactions, bookings, emails, AI responses, or payment confirmations.
10. Never use localStorage, mock databases, or temporary JSON files as production transactional persistence.
11. Do not weaken authentication, authorization, MFA, RLS, or security policies to make tests pass.
12. Do not modify production records, apply production migrations, enable live payments, merge into main, or deploy without explicit owner authorization.
13. Do not claim 100% completion while external integrations or production acceptance remain unverified.
14. Implement real functionality rather than buttons that do not perform actions.
15. Preserve all existing customer and business data.

